NOTE: Follow this rule when creating or editing GitHub issues via `gh issue create` / `gh issue edit`, drafting briefs under `docs/issues/`, or implementing **features** / **fixes** under `modules/` and `deploy/`.

## Title notation

```
{semantic}/PPT-{NNN}: [{domain}] {Title in sentence case}
```

| Part | Values | Example |
|------|--------|---------|
| `semantic` | `feat`, `docs`, `ops`, `test`, `harden`, `fix` | `feat/PPT-034` |
| `PPT-{NNN}` | Next program ID; label must match (`PPT-032`) | `PPT-041` |
| `domain` | `[api]`, `[model]`, `[EPIC][api]` for epics only | `[model]` |
| Epic | Prefix domain with `[EPIC]` | `feat/PPT-032: [EPIC][api] …` |

**Do not** use `PPT-0##: semantic(api):` — semantic comes **before** the program ID.

```text
✅ feat/PPT-036: [api] Accounts and categories CRUD (v3 model)
✅ harden/PPT-041: [model] Harden v3 data model for API readiness
✅ feat/PPT-032: [EPIC][api] FastAPI MVP on v3 model + Supabase PostgreSQL
❌ PPT-039: ops(api): Supabase B1 production wiring
❌ feat(api): FastAPI MVP
```

## Labels

Apply the matching `PPT-{NNN}` label plus domain labels (`API`, `data model`, `CI/CD`, `documentation`, etc.).

## Code paths (feat / fix / harden)

| Semantic | Domain | Primary paths |
|----------|--------|---------------|
| `feat`, `harden` | `[model]` | `modules/model/src/`, `modules/model/tests/`, `modules/model/alembic/` |
| `feat`, `fix` | `[api]` | `modules/api/src/`, `modules/api/tests/` |
| `feat`, `fix` | `[registrar]` | `modules/registrar/src/`, `modules/registrar/tests/` |
| `ops`, `fix` | `[infra]` | `deploy/`, `docker/`, `.github/` |
| `test` | any | `modules/**/tests/`, `.github/workflows/` |

When closing code for a feature or fix, the PR/issue body should cite the touched paths under **Tasks / deliverables** or **References**.

## Body template (maximize clarity)

```markdown
**Parent program:** [#28](…) (PPT-031) · **Parent epic:** [#42](…) · **PPT-{NNN}** · **Step:** {N}

## Summary
One paragraph: what, why, scope boundary.

## Depends on
- [#34](…) (PPT-031-E) — migration
- [#51](…) (PPT-041) — model hardening (if API work)

## Blocks
- Linked child issues this unblocks

## Platform rule (B0 + B1)
Validate on Docker Postgres (B0) **and** Supabase pooler `:6543` (B1) before closing.

## Tasks / deliverables
- [ ] Concrete, testable checkbox per deliverable
- [ ] Group by layer (model / API / CI)

## {Domain} integration
- [ ] B0 acceptance
- [ ] B1 acceptance
- [ ] Env vars / docs updated (`.env.example`, README)

## Requirements traceability
| ID | Scope |
|----|-------|
| FR-07 | … |
| NFR-04 | … |

## Out of scope
Bullet list — prevents scope creep (B2/B3, v4, DuckDB).

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] Measurable done conditions

## References
- Design docs, audit comments, parent epic
```

## Epic-specific additions

- Mermaid dependency graph (phases: design → migration → hardening → API → post-MVP)
- Sub-issue checklist with `PPT-{NNN} / #{issue}` links
- Prerequisites (gates G1–G7, PPT-031-E, PPT-041)
- **Blocked by** line at footer

## Program hierarchy (PPT-031)

| Layer | Example |
|-------|---------|
| Epic | [#28](https://github.com/Elmorralito/save-ma-money/issues/28) PPT-031 |
| Design tracks | PPT-031-A…E (#30–#34) |
| Model hardening | PPT-041 (#51) — blocks API epic |
| API epic | PPT-032 (#42) |
